# RepForge — AGENTS.md

Follow `/AGENTS.md` for all work in this repository. Non-negotiable summary:

## Before writing code
1. Search for existing components, hooks, utilities, types, and services.
2. Prefer **Reuse → Extend → Compose → Create**.
3. Do not copy-paste screens or duplicate headers/metrics/terminals/actions.

## Architecture
- Screens orchestrate; components present; hooks own reusable state/behavior; domain modules own pure logic.
- Stay consistent with existing folders: `src/app`, `src/features`, `src/shared`, `src/database`.
- Prefer feature-local modules when an experiment grows (constants, types, hooks) — do not dump everything in one giant screen file.

## Design system
- Use tokens from `src/app/theme` (`colors`, `spacing`, `radii`, `typography`, `categoryColors`).
- Reuse primitives from `src/shared/components`; compose feature-specific content.
- Do not invent one-off colors, radii, or button styles when tokens/components exist.

## Quality
- No `any` without a documented reason; prefer discriminated unions for experiment state.
- Keep business logic out of JSX; extract to hooks/utilities.
- Prefer screens under ~200 lines; split by responsibility when larger.
- Validate with TypeScript + ESLint before finishing.
- Leave the codebase cleaner than you found it.
